\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 A useful way to hold the whole profile\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Rather than interpreting the results as \'93I am high in X,\'94 try this:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \'93Under certain conditions, I may be more likely to become strategically focused, emotionally detached, or outcome-driven. I also appear to have meaningful capacities for empathy, humility, and ethical reflection. My development task is to make those protective capacities reliable under pressure.\'94
\f0\b0 \
That framing keeps the focus on 
\f1\b choice, context, behaviour, and accountability
\f0\b0 , rather than identity labels.\
Finally, treat self-assessment scores cautiously: questionnaire results can be influenced by the specific instrument, norms, mood, interpretation of questions, and self-presentation. They are not clinical diagnoses or fixed descriptions of your personality. Use them for reflection rather than labeling yourself or others, and respect colleagues' privacy, dignity, and right not to be psychologically profiled.\
